# Everything Git recognises as text is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf on a Windows clone hands the working tree CRLF
# while the repository holds LF — and Prettier, whose endOfLine default is lf,
# then reports every single file as badly formatted. `nx format:check` becomes
# noise no one can act on, which is how it came to be ignored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts and images are byte-for-byte; never let Git touch their line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
